      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "It looks like the game jumped ahead to combat and my Glider Staff never got cast, with Deserters showing as 2/3. Assessing the board, the opponent has an untapped Trebuchet, a vigilant 2/2 Parrot, and a summoning-sick 2/2 Parrot that can still block, all lands tapped with no tricks available, opponent at 12 life — so I'm considering attacking with Deserters and other creatures.\n\
\n\
Running the numbers on blocking scenarios, likely 2-5 damage gets through depending on how they assign blockers. On the crackback, their two flying Parrots plus a Boulder could deal 6 to me, putting me at 7 then potentially 1 — it's tight, but I could cast Staff and equip it postcombat to start blocking fliers, and using Airbend on their Trebuchet would remove a blocker and cut off their Boulder generation.\n\
\n\
If tokens attack alongside everything, Parrots would rather eat the tokens than trade with real creatures, meaning more damage slips through overall even though I lose the tokens; leaving tokens home doesn't help since they can't block a flying Boulder anyway, so tokens are purely attackers here.\n\
\n\
After combat I'll airbend the Trebuchet and equip Warriors, setting up next turn's swings against their two untapped Parrots. Weighing it out, tokens have some future value for spreading out blockers once Trebuchet's gone, but attacking with everything now still seems fine since the extra damage matters more than preserving a couple marginal tokens.\n\
\n\
